# 🏥 NHS Referral to Treatment (RTT) Waiting Times Analysis

## Overview
End-to-end data analysis of NHS England waiting times across 10 specialties and 7 regions (2020–2024), examining the impact of COVID-19 on patient waiting lists and recovery progress.

## Key Findings
- 📉 Average % seen within 18 weeks dropped to **73.1%** — well below the NHS 92% target
- 📈 Peak 52+ week waiters reached **54,181** during COVID recovery phase
- 🏥 **Ophthalmology and Gastroenterology** had the longest average waits
- 🗺️ **South West and Midlands** consistently underperformed on 18-week targets
- ✅ Clear recovery trend visible from mid-2021 onward

## Project Structure
```
nhs-waiting-times/
├── data/
│   ├── nhs_waiting_times.csv    # Generated dataset (3,990 records)
│   └── nhs_analysis.png         # Output visualisation
├── notebooks/
